      "excerpt": "Musically, \"Crazy\" was inspired by film scores of Spaghetti Westerns, in particular by the works of Ennio Morricone, and the song \"Last Men Standing\" by Gian Piero Reverberi and Gian Franco Reverberi from the 1968 Spaghetti Western Django, Prepare a Coffin, an unofficial prequel to Django \"Django (1966 film)\"). \"Crazy\" samples the song, and also utilizes parts of the main melody and chord structure. Because of this, the Reverberis are credited as songwriters along with CeeLo Green and Danger [.…",
